Recommends: qemu-efi-aarch64
Architecture: arm64
Description: NVIDIA's QEMU fork - AArch64 system emulator (local install)
 NVIDIA's QEMU fork providing AArch64 system emulation with KVM acceleration.
 .
 This package installs to /usr/local to avoid conflicts with system QEMU packages.
 .
 QEMU is a fast processor emulator: currently the package supports
 AArch64 emulation. By using dynamic translation it achieves
 reasonable speed while being easy to port on new host CPUs.
 .
 This package provides the system emulation for AArch64, in which
 a complete AArch64 system is emulated in a virtual machine.
 .
 Features enabled:
  - KVM acceleration for better performance
  - Vhost networking for efficient network I/O
  - Device Tree support for ARM systems
  - SLIRP networking for user-mode networking
  - Debug symbols for troubleshooting
 .
 The executable will be available as qemu-system-aarch64 in /usr/local/bin
 .
 It is recommended to also install qemu-efi-aarch64 for UEFI firmware support.
